              %p Here:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    (1a) and (1b) are equivalent expressions of the same morphism
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                    in
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒟
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi L
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi b
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}_{/L(b)}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjuncts"} adjuncts
                    between
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒟
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                    and (at the bottom) by the
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identity"} triangle identity
                %li
                  %p
                    (2a) and (2b) are equivalent expression of the same morphism
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mover
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
                    in
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi b
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/b}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
                    of the
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %p Hence:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    starting with a morphism as in (1a) and transforming it to
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2)
                    and then to (1b) is the identity operation;
                %li
                  %p starting with a morphism as in (2b) and transforming it to (1) and then to (2a) is the identity operation.
              %p
                In conclusion, the transformations (1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ↔
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leftrightarrow
                (2) consitute a
                %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#InTermsOfHomIsomorphism"} hom-isomorphism
                that witnesses an adjunction of the first claimed form
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SlicedAdjointFunctorsOverLb"} (1)
              %p
                %br/
              %p
                The
                %strong second case
                follows analogously, but a little more directly since no pullback is involved:
              %p
                %strong (1a)
